  "verbalization": "N-methylscopolamine is shown to have a target relationship with SMMC-7721 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 and other molecular targets. The first pathway links N-methylscopolamine to H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which is then targeted by (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-(Hydroxymethyl)-6-[3-[(E)-3-Hydroxyprop-1-Enyl]-2,5-Dimethoxyphenoxy]Oxane-3,4,5-Triol, a compound that ultimately targets SMMC-7721. The second pathway connects N-methylscopolamine directly to H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which is also targeted by 2,3-Didehydroalanine, another molecule that acts on SMMC-7721. The third pathway involves N-methylscopolamine targeting Prelamin-A/C, which is then targeted by Pseudopterosin Q, which also acts on SMMC-7721. These findings suggest that N-methylscopolamine may exert its effects through multiple molecular mechanisms, potentially involving ion transport and protein interaction, which could contribute to its interaction with SMMC-7721. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism of action involving the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, with the other targets providing additional layers of evidence for the drug's interaction with the cancer cell line.",
